<title>SWITZERLAND: Novartis sees positive Q2 currency effect.</title>
<headline>Novartis sees positive Q2 currency effect.</headline>
<dateline>ST. GALLEN, Switzerland 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daniel Vasella, chief executive of Swiss health sciences group Novartis AG, said second quarter results of Novartis would be favourably affected by the Swiss franc's exchange rate.</p>
<p>Vasella also told reporters at the St. Gallen Management Symposium that Novartis was on track for better 1997 earnings.</p>
</text>
